/* epstool.doc */

1994-03-24

epstool is not yet finished.

The documentation below is not complete and may be incorrect.

Works on little-endian machines (Intel).
May work on big-endian (Sun, Motorola), but has not had much testing.
  In particular, I haven't tested the TIFF output.

Purpose: Add EPSI or DOS EPS previews.
         Extract postscript from DOS EPS files.

- To work under OS/2, Unix and possibly MS-DOS.
- Uses Ghostscript to create preview bitmaps.
- Scan bmp file to find bounding box.
- Create TIFF or Interchange from part of BMP file.
- output to stdout or file.
- input must be from file.
- Options:
   input file,                 (on command line)
	DONE
   output file,                -o filename  or -ofilename
	Half done.  Need to put stdout into binary mode.
   page number,                -n pagenumber
	DONE
   resolution,                 -r dpi
	DONE
   calculate bounding box,     -b
	no support at all
   gs command,                 -gcommand or -g command
	DONE
- Operations:  
   Add TIFF 4,                  -t4 or -t
   Add TIFF 5,                  -t5
   Add Interchange,             -i
	Need to extract part of bitmap
   Extract PostScript,          -p
	DONE
   Extract Preview,             -v
	DONE

On-line help says:
Usage:  epstool [option] operation filename
  Options:
     -b             Calculate BoundingBox from image
     -g command     Ghostscript command
     -n number      Page number to extract
     -o filename    Output filename
     -r number      Preview resolution in dpi
  Operations: (one only)
     -i             Add Interchange preview (EPSI)
     -t4            Add TIFF4 preview       (DOS EPS)
     -t5            Add TIFF5 preview       (DOS EPS)
     -p             Extract PostScript      (DOS EPS)
     -v             Extract Preview         (DOS EPS)

